==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_OperationAuthorized  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_OperationAuthorized.als
    rationale: Removing the success-implies-allowed fact lets Alloy invent a successful customer DecideApp operation, which directly contradicts the permission matrix in the contract.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_002_CustomerScope
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_002_CustomerScope: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Clearing the matrix closed-world fact lets Allowed contain unauthorised cells; the injection then forces a forbidden customer audit-trail grant, which violates FR-021 and the deny side of the matrix.
    expected to FAIL: PermissionCompleteness, FR_021_OfficerHidden, FR_023_ComplianceReadOnly
      - PermissionCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_021_OfficerHidden: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_023_ComplianceReadOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoDuplicateEvents  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_NoDuplicateEvents.als
    rationale: Removing the no-duplicate-events fact and injecting two audit entries on the same application with the same newStatus directly demonstrates the append-only / one-per-change invariant breaking.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_018_AppendOnly, FR_019_OneAuditPerChange
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_019_OneAuditPerChange: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditMatchesJourney  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AuditMatchesJourney.als
    rationale: Clearing the journey-match fact lets an Approved application exist without the full chain of audit entries; the injection forces such an under-audited decided application to exist.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_017_AuditEveryChange
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_017_AuditEveryChange: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CustomerViewsOwn  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_CustomerViewsOwn.als
    rationale: Removing the customer-views-own constraint and injecting a successful ViewApp by a customer against an application owned by another customer is exactly the breach FR-020 forbids.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_020_CustomerSeeOwn
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_020_CustomerSeeOwn: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_NoLeakage  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_NoLeakage.als
    rationale: Removing the no-leakage fact lets the system return PermissionDenied to a customer probing a non-owned reference, revealing existence — exactly what FR-020's 404-not-403 rule forbids.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAttribution  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AuditAttribution.als
    rationale: Clearing the attribution fact and injecting a decide-event whose actor isn't the assigned officer produces a misattributed audit entry, breaking the FR-017 / attribution-correctness invariant.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)

